---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for InfluenzaSymptoms.com. How we handle your data in compliance with GDPR and Swedish data protection laws."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: July 2026</em></p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      InfluenzaSymptoms.com ("we," "us," "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains
      how we collect, use, and protect your personal data when you visit our website, in compliance
      with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable Swedish data protection laws.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this Privacy Policy or your data, contact us at the email address provided
      on our Contact page.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect minimal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Automatically collected:</strong> IP address, browser type, device information, pages visited, and referral sources — via privacy-focused analytics that do not use tracking cookies</li>
      <li><strong>Voluntarily provided:</strong> If you contact us, we collect your name, email address, and any information you choose to share</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect sensitive health data about our visitors.</p>

    <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To operate and improve the website</li>
      <li>To understand how visitors use our content (analytics)</li>
      <li>To respond to inquiries</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> Website operation and anonymous analytics</li>
      <li><strong>Consent:</strong> Where required by law (e.g., cookie consent if applicable)</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> Compliance with applicable laws</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which is privacy-focused and does not use
      tracking cookies. We do not use third-party advertising cookies or tracking pixels.
      If this changes, we will update this policy and implement a cookie consent mechanism.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal data. We may share data with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (hosting/CDN provider — processes access logs)</li>
      <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> if required by law</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics data is retained in aggregate form. Contact form submissions are retained
      for as long as needed to respond and for record-keeping purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access your personal data</li>
      <li>Rectify inaccurate data</li>
      <li>Erase your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
      <li>Restrict processing</li>
      <li>Data portability</li>
      <li>Object to processing</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, contact us. You also have the right to lodge a complaint
      with the Swedish Data Protection Authority (IMY — Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten) at <a href="https://www.imy.se">www.imy.se</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
